        "source_type": "text",
        "source_sentence": "Table I presents inherent viscosity data of polycarbonates from two-phase phase-transfer-catalyzed polycondensation of bisphenols with TCF at 25°C. The inherent viscosities of all polymers were in the range of 0.77 to 0.18 dL/g. Bisphenol A (PC-1) favors the highest inherent viscosity; the reason may be that bisphenol A having an electron releasing group increases the nucleophilicity."
      },
